617 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (How It Works : 1. Server Setup - A Node.js server is created using Express.js. Socket.IO is initialized to handle real-time communication. 2. Ngrok Integration - Ngrok is installed and started to expose the local server. It generates a public URL that clients can use to connect remotely. 3. Client-Side Connection -The frontend \(HTML, CSS, JavaScript\) connects to the Socket.IO server.A unique room ID is used to group users in the same session. 4. Real-Time Code Synchronization - When a user types in the editor, an event is sent to the server.The server broadcasts this update to all users in the same room.Other users receive the update and apply it to their editors. 5. Multi-User Collaboration - Users can join or leave rooms dynamically. Changes made by any user in the room are reflected for all participants.)
/E (How It Works : 1. Server Setup - A Node.js server is created using Express.js. Socket.IO is initialized to handle real-time communication. 2. Ngrok Integration - Ngrok is installed and started to expose the local server. It generates a public URL that clients can use to connect remotely. 3. Client-Side Connection -The frontend \(HTML, CSS, JavaScript\) connects to the Socket.IO server.A unique room ID is used to group users in the same session. 4. Real-Time Code Synchronization - When a user types in the editor, an event is sent to the server.The server broadcasts this update to all users in the same room.Other users receive the update and apply it to their editors. 5. Multi-User Collaboration - Users can join or leave rooms dynamically. Changes made by any user in the room are reflected for all participants.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
